  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published method apply assay-aware, paired, and reinforcement learning models to selectivity and ligand construction.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is machine learning used to prioritize small molecules by activity and selectivity. D2ML builds assay-aware models predicting activity and selectivity from crude and purified direct-to-biology screening data, with ROS1 as a guiding case. A paired-activity regression and SVM workflow screens 12 million molecules to identify mutant-selective EGFR triple-mutant inhibitors, supported by two crystal structures. Two ADMET benchmarks test protocol-matched choices: active-learning acquisition strategies across eight regression endpoints, and GNNs versus frozen pretrained models and fingerprints on six TDC endpoints under scaffold splits. PSICHIC+ applies a bioactivity foundation model trained on about 82M protein-ligand records to hit identification. FragDockRL instead addresses ligand construction, using DQN-based reinforcement learning over building-block assembly with tethered docking. The new elements are paired or assay-aware training, rigorous benchmarking, and RL-driven fragment assembly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
